# Rank 1506 / CVE-2026-38429: OpenCMS's older import versions unmarshalled an
# uploaded manifest with no entity resolver, so external entities in the
# import archive are fetched (CWE-611). CmsImportVersion2 through 5 and
# CmsXmlPageConverter all called CmsXmlUtils.unmarshalHelper(bytes, null);
# the core overload (CmsXmlUtils.java:817) builds a dom4j SAXReader, calls
# reader.setEntityResolver(resolver) only when the resolver is non-null, and
# reads -- so a null resolver left the parser's default entity resolution in
# place and file:///http:///opencms:// references in the manifest resolved
# externally. The fixing commit ("Fixed XXE
# vulnerability in older import versions."): every unmarshalHelper call in
# CmsImportVersion2/3/4/5 and CmsXmlPageConverter now passes
# new CmsXmlEntityResolver(null), whose resolveEntity() answers only from
# internal caches, the classpath XMLPAGE DTD/XSD, the opencms:// VFS scheme
# and the internal: scheme, and throws "Entity reference not allowed" for
# everything else. .
#
# FIXED by a sink binding. # The import versions' own digester sites are
# reported (VYQL-DESER-002 at CmsImportVersion7/10 through
# digester.parse), but the unmarshalHelper sites stay invisible: the call
# is a static helper in another package (org.opencms.xml), taint does not
# cross package boundaries into the wrapper, and no binding labelled the
# helper itself. vyql/bindings/java/mxmlentityresolver.vyql emits
# code.XmlParse at unmarshalHelper's first argument -- the method is
# documented as unmarshalling XML, and any method of that name does.
# Measured on the real code (src/org/opencms/importexport): the vulnerable
# revision goes from 6 to 13 VYQL-DESER-002 findings, adding exactly this
# commit's call sites -- CmsImportVersion2.java:191 and :833,
# CmsImportVersion3.java:127, CmsImportVersion4.java:132,
# CmsImportVersion5.java:143, CmsXmlPageConverter.java:79 and
# A_CmsImport.java:345 -- each with source code.HttpInput at
# CmsImportHelper (the uploaded import archive) and the unless clauses
# unsatisfied. The fixed revision's own control is not expressible, recorded rather
# than papered over: distinguishing unmarshalHelper(x, null) from
# unmarshalHelper(x, new CmsXmlEntityResolver(null)) needs an argument-
# shape predicate, java's null_literal lowers to Const without a Value
# (internal/extract/frontend/treesitter/java.go) and args.any.path is not
# implemented in the scanner IR lowering (internal/bindings/
# compile_shapes.go), so the binding cannot condition on the resolver's
# presence and the fixed revision still reports at the call sites -- the
# same shape-survives-the-fix family as rank 1503. Entered in
# ENGINE-GAPS.md as a mechanical gap with the minimal pair below: the
# expect case reports, the reject case (same call, resolver passed) should
# not but does. The spec's reject direction therefore pins the boundary
# the rule can draw today, following the rank 232 precedent: bytes that
# are read but never handed to an XML parser report nothing.
#
# verify_current_expected: fixed-sink-binding

test "rank1506: the import manifest is unmarshalled with no entity resolver"
  lang java
  file src/org/opencms/importexport/CmsImportVersion2.java
  expect VYQL-DESER-002
  code
  ```
  package org.opencms.importexport;

  import jakarta.ws.rs.FormParam;
  import jakarta.ws.rs.POST;

  public class CmsImportVersion2 {
    @POST
    public void importManifest(@FormParam("file") byte[] manifest) throws Exception {
      org.dom4j.Document doc = CmsXmlUtils.unmarshalHelper(manifest, null);
      doc.getRootElement().getName();
    }
  }
  ```

test "rank1506: uploaded bytes that never reach an xml parser report nothing"
  lang java
  file src/org/opencms/importexport/CmsImportVersion2.java
  reject VYQL-DESER-002
  code
  ```
  package org.opencms.importexport;

  import jakarta.ws.rs.FormParam;
  import jakarta.ws.rs.POST;

  public class CmsImportVersion2 {
    @POST
    public String importManifest(@FormParam("file") byte[] manifest) throws Exception {
      int total = 0;
      for (byte b : manifest) {
        total += b;
      }
      return Integer.toString(total);
    }
  }
  ```
